   "Buffalo.AG.Part08.prop_584"
  ],
  "index_key": "vuys5SNs2eQ-584",
  "note": "The equivalence needs Y regular of dimension one (as in item 327 above and index entry 584): the normalization of a nodal curve is reduced, its component dominates, and it is not flat. Proved: affine form over a Dedekind ring (prop_584, and prop_587 for associated points).",
  "correction": {
   "old": "$X$ reduced over $Y$ of dimension one: $X$ flat over $Y$ $\\iff$ every irreducible component of $X$ dominates (a component of) $Y$. In general: every associated cycle dominates.",
   "new": "$X$ reduced over $Y$ regular of dimension one: $X$ flat over $Y$ $\\iff$ every irreducible component of $X$ dominates (a component of) $Y$. In general: every associated cycle dominates."
  }
 },
 {
  "board": "vuys5SNs2eQ-0000.json",
  "t": 712,
  "kind": "p",
  "status": "imprecise",
  "lean": [
   "Buffalo.AG.Part08.board_cex_712"
  ],
  "index_key": "vuys5SNs2eQ-712",
  "note": "Equal fibre dimensions alone do not give flatness: the line V(y) ⊂ 𝔸² has all non-empty fibres of dimension 0 but is not flat (board_cex_712 proves non-flatness). The criterion (index entry 712) asks for the expected dimension dim X − dim Y; possibly an oral shorthand for this. Cohen–Macaulay rings are not in mathlib.",
  "correction": {
   "old": "$Y$ regular, $f$ of finite type, $X$ Cohen–Macaulay (e.g. regular): $f$ flat $\\iff$ all fibres (all components of fibres) have the same dimension.",
   "new": "$Y$ regular, $f$ of finite type, $X$ Cohen–Macaulay (e.g. regular): $f$ flat $\\iff$ all fibres (all components of fibres) have the expected dimension $\\dim X-\\dim Y$."
  }
 },
