 {
  "board": "vuys5SNs2eQ-11745.json",
  "t": 13450,
  "kind": "p",
  "status": "false",
  "lean": [],
  "note": "Freeness does not descend along faithfully flat quasi-compact maps: a non-principal ideal of a Dedekind ring (e.g. (2, 1+√−5) in ℤ[√−5]) is not free but becomes free after A → ∏ A_{f_i} for a suitable Zariski covering. Locally free of rank n does descend (index entry 3556). The Lean counterexample (a non-free projective module) is not formalised. The other properties listed are covered by the index entries 2750, 3040, 3104, 3491, 3556, 5323, 5811, 12211.",
  "correction": {
   "old": "Properties that descend by faithfully flat quasi-compact base change: closed/open/quasi-compact immersion, proper, separated, finite type, locally of (finite) presentation, quasi-compact, quasi-separated, universally open, universally generalizing; for modules: finite type, finite presentation, free, locally free of rank $n$, invertible.",
   "new": "Properties that descend by faithfully flat quasi-compact base change: closed/open/quasi-compact immersion, proper, separated, finite type, locally of (finite) presentation, quasi-compact, quasi-separated, universally open, universally generalizing; for modules: finite type, finite presentation, locally free of rank $n$, invertible."
  }
 },
